      "tip": "On your **mother's side**:\n\n- **নানা / নানি**: grandfather / grandmother\n- **মামা / মামি**: mother's brother / his wife\n- **খালা / খালু**: mother's sister / her husband\n\nRemember by the first sound: **দাদা / দাদি** (*da-*) are your father's parents, **নানা / নানি** (*na-*) your mother's.\n\n'Mother's' is **মায়ের** (*mayer*). After most words ending in a vowel the possessive is just -র (বাবা → বাবার), but মা takes **-এর** with a little **য়** glide.\n\n**মামা** is also how you cheerfully address a rickshaw driver or the man at the tea stall (Lesson 6). Kolkata: maternal grandparents are দাদু / দিদিমা, mother's sister is মাসি.",
